       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 850 mg per dose for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Please tell me the dose and frequency.\n- **1,700 mg three times daily as written.** If this is deliberate, please confirm and give the rationale. I can then enter it with a note.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
